IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lca-juveniles`

-- Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA), Part 4 Division 9 and s 167 -- the Q&A layer: the questions people ask, with the seat
-- and the situation as parameters, so that one deployment serves every seat and the question form drops the questions
-- that do not arise.
--
-- SEATS (`my role`, the first input of every exported question, "Which of these describes you"):
--   * the young person, under 18 or about to turn 18 -- the baseline's seat, whose 25 questions are asked here by
--     calling the baseline's functions in lca-juveniles.l4;
--   * a parent, guardian or other adult with a young person -- who may supply liquor at home (s 122A), buy it for a
--     juvenile who asks (s 121(3)), take a juvenile on to premises as a responsible adult (ss 121(5)(a)(i), (9), 122(3)(b)),
--     or send one for liquor (s 124);
--   * the licensee, a manager, or a person who sells or serves liquor -- bound by ss 121(1), (4), (10) and 122(2), with
--     the defences of s 125(1)(b), (c), and holding the s 126 powers as an "authorised person" (s 3(1)).
-- A question about another role answers `does not arise for you` without reading any other input. The Director, an
-- inspector and the police are never seats: what they may do appears as what it means for the person asking.
--
-- SITUATIONS (design D8 of the graffiti encoding): within a role, a question that arises only in a situation takes that
-- situation's fact straight after `my role`, and when it does not hold answers `does not arise for you` without reading
-- anything else. The questions of one situation share one input, character for character. They are:
--   * for the young person: the area being declared out of bounds now (s 121(6)-(8)); an authorised person having asked
--     my age, or for evidence of it (s 126(1)(b), (2), (2a)); having been required to leave, or removed (s 126(4)); someone
--     having given or sold me alcohol, or offered to (ss 121(1), 122(2), 122A, 125(1)(b)); having been sent to get liquor
--     (s 124); working, or wanting to work, with liquor (s 121(10), (11));
--   * for the adult: having given, or being about to give, alcohol to a person under 18; being with one on licensed or
--     regulated premises; having sent, or being about to send, one for liquor;
--   * for the licensee or seller: a sale or supply to a person under 18; a person under 18 on the licensed premises;
--     employing one to serve liquor; suspecting that a person on the premises is under 18.
-- Two of the baseline's own inputs are situations here: `the area is declared out of bounds to juveniles now` and
-- `I was sent to get liquor`; where they hold, the baseline is called with them as they are. A question that arises in
-- every situation of its role (am I a juvenile, the offences of being somewhere or buying, carrying or drinking, the
-- fines) takes no situation input. Every situation input is a BOOLEAN, so no situation helper reads an enumeration
-- through OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31); the layer's own helpers over enumerations list every value.
--
-- No exported question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT input. Dates are numbers written YYYYMMDD, as in the baseline.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA), juveniles -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I am a young person (under 18, or about to turn 18)`
    `I am a parent, guardian or other adult with a young person`
    `I hold a licence, manage licensed premises, or sell or serve liquor`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Days` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    days HAS `number of days` IS A NUMBER

-- The adult's position, for s 122A(2) (the baseline's `Supplier`, from the adult's seat).
DECLARE `Who I am to the young person` IS ONE OF
    `their parent or guardian`
    `another adult, with their parent's or guardian's consent`
    `another adult, without that consent`

-- s 125(2)(b), from the adult's seat (the baseline's `Companion`, without `nobody`).
DECLARE `How I am related to the young person` IS ONE OF
    `their parent`
    `their step-parent`
    `their spouse or de facto partner`
    `their legal guardian`
    `another adult standing in place of their parent`
    `another adult or friend`

-- s 125(2)(b), from the licensee's seat (the baseline's `Companion`).
DECLARE `Who is with the young person` IS ONE OF
    `their parent`
    `their step-parent`
    `their spouse or de facto partner`
    `their legal guardian`
    `another adult standing in place of their parent`
    `another adult or friend`
    `nobody`

-- s 121(1)(a)-(d), s 122(2): who commits the offence when liquor is sold or supplied to a juvenile.
DECLARE `My part in the sale` IS ONE OF
    `the licensee`
    `the manager supervising the premises at the time`
    `the person who sold or supplied it`
    `a person who permitted it`
    `a staff member who had no part in it`

-- s 121(4)(a), (b): the licensee commits the offence whether or not they permitted the young person's presence; a
-- manager, as the licensee's employee or agent, only if they permitted it ((b)). The two facts, the position and the
-- permission, are one input, since permission matters only for (b).
DECLARE `My part in the young person's presence` IS ONE OF
    `I am the licensee`
    `I am a manager, employee or agent of the licensee, and I permitted the person to enter or stay`
    `I am a manager, employee or agent of the licensee, and I did not permit it`

-- The adult's offences in Division 9, with the penalties printed in the deposited text.
DECLARE `Adult offence` IS ONE OF
    `supplying liquor to a person under 18 on licensed premises (s 121(1)(c))`
    `permitting the sale or supply to a person under 18 on licensed premises (s 121(1)(d))`
    `buying liquor on licensed premises for a person under 18 at their request (s 121(3))`
    `leaving a person under 18 on licensed premises without telling the licensee or staff (s 121(9))`
    `supplying, or permitting supply, drinking or possession by, a person under 18 on regulated premises or a road (s 122(2))`
    `taking a person under 18 into regulated premises as a responsible adult, other than for a meal (s 122(3)(b))`
    `supplying liquor to a person under 18 on unlicensed premises in breach of s 122A`
    `sending a person under 18 to get liquor (s 124)`

-- The licensee's and seller's offences in Division 9, with the penalties printed in the deposited text.
DECLARE `Business offence` IS ONE OF
    `selling or supplying to a person under 18 on licensed premises, as the licensee or a manager (s 121(1)(a), (b))`
    `selling or supplying to a person under 18 on licensed premises, as another seller (s 121(1)(c))`
    `permitting a sale or supply to a person under 18 on licensed premises (s 121(1)(d))`
    `permitting a person under 18 to drink on licensed premises, as the licensee or a manager (s 121(2)(a))`
    `permitting a person under 18 to drink on licensed premises, as anyone else (s 121(2)(b))`
    `a person under 18 on licensed premises, as the licensee, or a manager who permitted it (s 121(4)(a), (b))`
    `a person under 18 on licensed premises, as another employee or agent who permitted it (s 121(4)(b))`
    `employing a person under 18 to sell, supply or serve liquor (s 121(10))`
    `selling, supplying or permitting it on regulated premises or a road (s 122(2))`

§§ `Carrying the baseline's answers, and the helpers the new seats need`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

GIVEN `the number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`as an amount` `the number` MEANS amount `the number`

GIVEN `the number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Days`
`as days` `the number` MEANS days `the number`

-- The helpers below that read an enumeration list every value, with no OTHERWISE.
GIVEN `who I am` IS A `Who I am to the young person`
GIVETH A Supplier
`the supplier for` `who I am` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who I am`
    WHEN `their parent or guardian` THEN `my parent or guardian`
    WHEN `another adult, with their parent's or guardian's consent` THEN `another person, with my parent's or guardian's consent`
    WHEN `another adult, without that consent` THEN `another person, without that consent`

GIVEN `the relation` IS A `How I am related to the young person`
GIVETH A Companion
`the companion for` `the relation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the relation`
    WHEN `their parent` THEN `my parent`
    WHEN `their step-parent` THEN `my step-parent`
    WHEN `their spouse or de facto partner` THEN `my spouse or de facto partner`
    WHEN `their legal guardian` THEN `my legal guardian`
    WHEN `another adult standing in place of their parent` THEN `another adult standing in place of my parent`
    WHEN `another adult or friend` THEN `another adult or friend`

GIVEN `who is with them` IS A `Who is with the young person`
GIVETH A Companion
`the companion of theirs for` `who is with them` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who is with them`
    WHEN `their parent` THEN `my parent`
    WHEN `their step-parent` THEN `my step-parent`
    WHEN `their spouse or de facto partner` THEN `my spouse or de facto partner`
    WHEN `their legal guardian` THEN `my legal guardian`
    WHEN `another adult standing in place of their parent` THEN `another adult standing in place of my parent`
    WHEN `another adult or friend` THEN `another adult or friend`
    WHEN `nobody` THEN `nobody`

-- s 121(9): "Where a person or juvenile is lawfully on licensed premises by reason of being in the company and under the
-- supervision of a responsible adult, if that adult leaves the juvenile on the licensed premises deprived of his or her
-- company and supervision without first informing the licensee or an employee or agent of the licensee the adult
-- commits an offence." The adult is taken to be 18 or over, as the role says.
GIVEN `the companion` IS A Companion
      `supervising` IS A BOOLEAN
      `leaves` IS A BOOLEAN
      `told first` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 121(9) -- the responsible adult leaves the juvenile behind` IF
        `is a responsible adult` `the companion` TRUE
    AND `supervising`
    AND `leaves`
    AND (NOT `told first`)

-- s 122(3)(b): "being a person who has purported to accompany the juvenile as a responsible adult for the purpose of
-- obtaining a meal, causes or permits the juvenile to enter or remain in any part of regulated premises where liquor is
-- sold or supplied, except for the purpose of permitting the juvenile to obtain a meal", where the juvenile is not an
-- employee or agent (s 122(3)), and not within s 120(1)(b), (f), 120(2) or 121(5)(c), (d) (s 122(4)). Those conditions are
-- the juvenile's own under s 122(3)(a), which the baseline's question decides.
GIVEN `the reason` IS A Reason
      `liquor sold there` IS A BOOLEAN
      `works there` IS A BOOLEAN
      `came for a meal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `caused or permitted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 122(3)(b) -- the purported responsible adult commits the offence` IF
        `came for a meal`
    AND `caused or permitted`
    AND `Is it an offence for me to be on regulated premises` `the reason` `liquor sold there` `works there`

-- s 121(1): where liquor is sold or supplied to a juvenile on licensed premises, "(a) the licensee; and (b) any manager who
-- is supervising and managing the licensed premises at the time ...; and (c) any other person by whom the liquor is sold or
-- supplied; and (d) any person who permits the sale or supply, each commit an offence". s 122(2): on regulated premises,
-- and on a road (s 122(1)(g)), "a person who (a) sells or supplies, or permits the sale or supply of, liquor to ... a
-- juvenile". Elsewhere neither applies (s 122A is not asked here).
GIVEN `the place` IS A Place
      `the part` IS A `My part in the sale`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 121(1), 122(2) -- the sale or supply to a juvenile is an offence of mine` IF
    CONSIDER `the place`
    WHEN `licensed premises` THEN
        CONSIDER `the part`
        WHEN `the licensee` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the manager supervising the premises at the time` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the person who sold or supplied it` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a person who permitted it` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a staff member who had no part in it` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `regulated premises` THEN `sells, supplies or permits` `the part`
    WHEN `a road or footpath` THEN `sells, supplies or permits` `the part`
    WHEN `another place the public can go` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a private home or other private place` THEN FALSE
    WHERE
        `sells, supplies or permits` p MEANS
            CONSIDER p
            WHEN `the licensee` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `the manager supervising the premises at the time` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `the person who sold or supplied it` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a person who permitted it` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a staff member who had no part in it` THEN FALSE

-- s 121(4): where a juvenile enters or remains on any part of licensed premises, "(a) the licensee; and (b) any employee
-- or agent of the licensee who permits the juvenile to enter or remain ...; and (c) the juvenile, each commit an offence",
-- subject to s 121(5). Only the licensee is named in (a): a manager is the licensee's employee or agent, and commits
-- the offence under (b) only by permitting it. The penalty's "(a) for the licensee or a manager" sets a manager's fine,
-- not who commits the offence (fixed 6 November 2026, after verification; see NOTES QA8).
GIVEN `my part` IS A `My part in the young person's presence`
      `the juvenile's presence is an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 121(4) -- the presence of the juvenile is an offence of mine` IF
    CONSIDER `my part`
    WHEN `I am the licensee` THEN `the juvenile's presence is an offence`
    WHEN `I am a manager, employee or agent of the licensee, and I permitted the person to enter or stay` THEN `the juvenile's presence is an offence`
    WHEN `I am a manager, employee or agent of the licensee, and I did not permit it` THEN FALSE

-- s 125(1)(c): "where the offence is alleged to have occurred on regulated premises, if the accused is the licensee or
-- occupier or a manager of the regulated premises and did not personally sell or supply the liquor, that -- (i) the
-- business was not conducted in such a way as to entice juveniles ...; and (ii) that proper diligence was exercised".
GIVEN `the place` IS A Place
      `licensee, occupier or manager` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sold it personally` IS A BOOLEAN
      `not enticing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `diligent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 125(1)(c) -- the defence for regulated premises` IF
        `on regulated premises`
    AND `licensee, occupier or manager`
    AND (NOT `sold it personally`)
    AND `not enticing`
    AND `diligent`
    WHERE
        `on regulated premises` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the place`
            WHEN `licensed premises` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `regulated premises` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a road or footpath` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `another place the public can go` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `a private home or other private place` THEN FALSE

-- The adult's maximum fines: ss 121(1)(c) "(b) for the sale or supply by any other person, a fine of $6 000", (d) "(c) for
-- anyone else, a fine of $3 000"; 121(3) $2 000; 121(9) $3 000; 122(2) $15 000; 122(3)(b) "(b) for anyone else, a fine of
-- $6 000"; 122A(2), (3) $10 000; 124 $3 000.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Adult offence`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most an adult can be fined for` `the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `supplying liquor to a person under 18 on licensed premises (s 121(1)(c))` THEN 6000
    WHEN `permitting the sale or supply to a person under 18 on licensed premises (s 121(1)(d))` THEN 3000
    WHEN `buying liquor on licensed premises for a person under 18 at their request (s 121(3))` THEN 2000
    WHEN `leaving a person under 18 on licensed premises without telling the licensee or staff (s 121(9))` THEN 3000
    WHEN `supplying, or permitting supply, drinking or possession by, a person under 18 on regulated premises or a road (s 122(2))` THEN 15000
    WHEN `taking a person under 18 into regulated premises as a responsible adult, other than for a meal (s 122(3)(b))` THEN 6000
    WHEN `supplying liquor to a person under 18 on unlicensed premises in breach of s 122A` THEN 10000
    WHEN `sending a person under 18 to get liquor (s 124)` THEN 3000

-- The licensee's and seller's maximum fines: s 121(1) $15 000 / $6 000 / $3 000; s 121(2) $15 000 / $6 000; s 121(4)
-- $15 000 / $6 000; s 121(10) $15 000; s 122(2) $15 000.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Business offence`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most a licensee or seller can be fined for` `the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `selling or supplying to a person under 18 on licensed premises, as the licensee or a manager (s 121(1)(a), (b))` THEN 15000
    WHEN `selling or supplying to a person under 18 on licensed premises, as another seller (s 121(1)(c))` THEN 6000
    WHEN `permitting a sale or supply to a person under 18 on licensed premises (s 121(1)(d))` THEN 3000
    WHEN `permitting a person under 18 to drink on licensed premises, as the licensee or a manager (s 121(2)(a))` THEN 15000
    WHEN `permitting a person under 18 to drink on licensed premises, as anyone else (s 121(2)(b))` THEN 6000
    WHEN `a person under 18 on licensed premises, as the licensee, or a manager who permitted it (s 121(4)(a), (b))` THEN 15000
    WHEN `a person under 18 on licensed premises, as another employee or agent who permitted it (s 121(4)(b))` THEN 6000
    WHEN `employing a person under 18 to sell, supply or serve liquor (s 121(10))` THEN 15000
    WHEN `selling, supplying or permitting it on regulated premises or a road (s 122(2))` THEN 15000

§§ `For the young person (the baseline's seat)`

-- Each question calls the baseline's function of the same subject (lca-juveniles.l4) and restates no rule: for this
-- role, and where its situation holds, its answer is the baseline's, carried in the answer types above.

§§§ `s 3(1) -- am I a juvenile, and may I buy and drink alcohol now`

@export Am I a juvenile -- under 18 -- for the Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) (s 3(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my date of birth` IS A NUMBER @desc Your date of birth, written YYYYMMDD
      `the date` IS A NUMBER @desc The date in question, written YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I under 18 for the Liquor Control Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a young person (under 18, or about to turn 18)` THEN `yes if` (`Am I a juvenile` `my date of birth` `the date`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I buy and drink alcohol here now without committing a juvenile offence (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) ss 3(1), 123)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my date of birth` IS A NUMBER @desc Your date of birth, written YYYYMMDD
      `the date` IS A NUMBER @desc The date in question, written YYYYMMDD
      `the place` IS A Place @desc Where you are (or were)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I buy and drink alcohol here now without a juvenile offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a young person (under 18, or about to turn 18)` THEN `yes if` (`May I buy and drink alcohol here now` `my date of birth` `the date` `the place`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 120-123 -- being on licensed or regulated premises, and buying, carrying and drinking`

@export Is it an offence for me to be on these licensed premises (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) s 121(4), (5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the reason` IS A Reason @desc Why you are there
      `who is with me` IS A Companion @desc Who is with you
      `they are an adult` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person with you is an adult (18 or over)
      `I am under their supervision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that person is supervising you while you are there
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is it an offence for me to be on these licensed premises` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a young person (under 18, or about to turn 18)` THEN `yes if` (`Is it an offence for me to be on licensed premises` `the reason` `who is with me` `they are an adult` `I am under their supervision`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I be made to leave this out-of-bounds area of licensed premises (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) s 121(6)-(8))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the area is declared out of bounds to juveniles now` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether notices at the entrance declare the area out of bounds to juveniles at this time
      `the reason` IS A Reason @desc Why you are there
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I be made to leave this out-of-bounds area` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a young person (under 18, or about to turn 18)` THEN
        IF `the area is declared out of bounds to juveniles now`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can I be made to leave an out-of-bounds area` `the reason` `the area is declared out of bounds to juveniles now`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Have I committed an offence by not leaving the out-of-bounds area (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) s 121(7))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the area is declared out of bounds to juveniles now` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether notices at the entrance declare the area out of bounds to juveniles at this time
      `the reason` IS A Reason @desc Why you are there
      `an authorised person required me to leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an authorised person told you to leave
      `I left` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you left when told
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Have I committed an offence by not leaving this out-of-bounds area` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a young person (under 18, or about to turn 18)` THEN
        IF `the area is declared out of bounds to juveniles now`
        THEN `yes if` (`Have I committed an offence by not leaving` `the reason` `the area is declared out of bounds to juveniles now` `an authorised person required me to leave` `I left`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is it an offence for me to be in this part of regulated premises (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) s 122(3), (4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the reason` IS A Reason @desc Why you are there
      `liquor is sold or supplied in that part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether liquor is sold or supplied in the part of the premises where you are
      `I work for the licensee, occupier or a contractor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an employee or agent of the licensee or occupier, or of someone working under a contract with them
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is it an offence for me to be in this part of regulated premises` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a young person (under 18, or about to turn 18)` THEN `yes if` (`Is it an offence for me to be on regulated premises` `the reason` `liquor is sold or supplied in that part` `I work for the licensee, occupier or a contractor`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is it an offence for me, as a juvenile, to buy or get liquor here, or try to (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) s 123(1)(a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the place` IS A Place @desc Where you are (or were)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is it an offence for me to buy or get liquor at this place` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a young person (under 18, or about to turn 18)` THEN `yes if` (`Is it an offence for me to buy or get liquor here` `the place`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is it an offence for me, as a juvenile, to have liquor with me here (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) s 123(1)(b), (2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the place` IS A Place @desc Where you are (or were)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is it an offence for me to have liquor with me at this place` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a young person (under 18, or about to turn 18)` THEN `yes if` (`Is it an offence for me to have liquor here` `the place`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is it an offence for me, as a juvenile, to drink liquor here (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) s 123(1)(c), (2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the place` IS A Place @desc Where you are (or were)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is it an offence for me to drink liquor at this place` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a young person (under 18, or about to turn 18)` THEN `yes if` (`Is it an offence for me to drink here` `the place`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Have I committed an offence by getting someone to buy liquor for me on licensed premises (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) s 121(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the place` IS A Place @desc Where you are (or were)
      `they bought or got it for me at my request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other person bought or got liquor for you because you asked
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Have I committed an offence by getting someone to buy liquor for me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a young person (under 18, or about to turn 18)` THEN `yes if` (`Have I committed an offence by getting someone to buy for me` `the place` `they bought or got it for me at my request`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 121(1), 122(2), 122A, 124, 125(1)(b) -- the person who gives me alcohol, or sends me for it`

@export Is it lawful for this person to give me alcohol here (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) ss 121(1), 122(2), 122A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `someone has given or sold me alcohol, or offered to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone has sold, supplied or given you alcohol, or has offered to
      `the place` IS A Place @desc Where you are (or were)
      `the supplier` IS A Supplier @desc Who is giving you the alcohol
      `my parent or guardian was drunk when consenting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your parent or guardian was drunk when they gave consent
      `the supplier is drunk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person giving it to you is drunk
      `I am drunk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are drunk
      `the supplier is able to supervise my drinking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person giving it to you can supervise you drinking it
      `a circumstance prescribed by the regulations applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a circumstance prescribed by the Liquor Control Regulations applies
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is it lawful for this person to give me alcohol at this place` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a young person (under 18, or about to turn 18)` THEN
        IF `someone has given or sold me alcohol, or offered to`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is it lawful for this person to give me alcohol here` `the place` `the supplier` `my parent or guardian was drunk when consenting` `the supplier is drunk` `I am drunk` `the supplier is able to supervise my drinking` `a circumstance prescribed by the regulations applies`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export If giving me alcohol was an offence, what is the most the person who gave it can be fined (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) ss 121(1), 122(2), 122A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `someone has given or sold me alcohol, or offered to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone has sold, supplied or given you alcohol, or has offered to
      `the place` IS A Place @desc Where you are (or were)
      `the role` IS A `Seller role` @desc Who sold or supplied it
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most the person who gave me alcohol can be fined` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a young person (under 18, or about to turn 18)` THEN
        IF `someone has given or sold me alcohol, or offered to`
        THEN `as an amount` (`What is the most the supplier can be fined` `the place` `the role`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Could the person who sold me liquor rely on believing I was 18 (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) s 125(1)(b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `someone has given or sold me alcohol, or offered to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone has sold, supplied or given you alcohol, or has offered to
      `my age when I was sold it` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years when you were sold it
      `they believed on reasonable grounds I was 18 or over` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller believed, on reasonable grounds, that you were 18 or over
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Could the person who sold me liquor rely on believing I was 18` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a young person (under 18, or about to turn 18)` THEN
        IF `someone has given or sold me alcohol, or offered to`
        THEN `yes if` (`Could the seller rely on believing I was 18` `my age when I was sold it` `they believed on reasonable grounds I was 18 or over`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Did the person who sent me to get liquor commit an offence (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) s 124)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I was sent to get liquor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were sent there to get liquor
      `the place` IS A Place @desc Where you are (or were)
      `they knew or believed I was under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who sent you knew or believed you were under 18
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Did the person who sent me to get liquor commit an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a young person (under 18, or about to turn 18)` THEN
        IF `I was sent to get liquor`
        THEN `yes if` (`Did the person who sent me commit an offence` `the place` `I was sent to get liquor` `they knew or believed I was under 18`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 121(10), (11) -- serving liquor at work`

@export May I be employed to sell, supply or serve liquor (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) s 121(10), (11))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I work, or want to work, selling, supplying or serving liquor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are employed or engaged, or want to be, to sell, supply or serve liquor on licensed premises or premises with an occasional licence or permit (s 121(10))
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years
      `only serving liquor with meals` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you would only serve liquor ancillary to a meal
      `the Director has approved my employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Director of Liquor Licensing has approved your employment
      `I am supervised at all times` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your work is supervised at all times
      `the work is assessed for, or I have completed, a prescribed training course` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work will be assessed for a prescribed training course you are doing, or you have completed one that assessed it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I be employed to sell, supply or serve liquor` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a young person (under 18, or about to turn 18)` THEN
        IF `I work, or want to work, selling, supplying or serving liquor`
        THEN `yes if` (`May I be employed to serve liquor` `my age` `only serving liquor with meals` `the Director has approved my employment` `I am supervised at all times` `the work is assessed for, or I have completed, a prescribed training course`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 126 -- proof of age`

@export Can I be required to state my age (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) s 126(1)(a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the place` IS A Place @desc Where you are (or were)
      `the authorised person knows or reasonably suspects I am under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the authorised person knows, or suspects on reasonable grounds, that you are under 18
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I be required to state my age here` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a young person (under 18, or about to turn 18)` THEN `yes if` (`Can I be required to state my age` `the place` `the authorised person knows or reasonably suspects I am under 18`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I be required to show evidence of my age (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) s 126(1)(b)(i))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `an authorised person has asked my age, or for evidence of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on licensed or regulated premises, the licensee, a manager, a staff member or a police officer has asked you to state your age or to show evidence of it (s 126)
      `the place` IS A Place @desc Where you are (or were)
      `the authorised person knows or reasonably suspects I am under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the authorised person knows, or suspects on reasonable grounds, that you are under 18
      `the age I stated is or appears false` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the age you stated is false, or appears to be false
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I be required to show evidence of my age here` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a young person (under 18, or about to turn 18)` THEN
        IF `an authorised person has asked my age, or for evidence of it`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can I be required to show evidence of my age` `the place` `the authorised person knows or reasonably suspects I am under 18` `the age I stated is or appears false`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does what I showed count as evidence of my age (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) s 126(1)(b)(i), (2C))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `an authorised person has asked my age, or for evidence of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on licensed or regulated premises, the licensee, a manager, a staff member or a police officer has asked you to state your age or to show evidence of it (s 126)
      `what I showed` IS AN Evidence @desc What you showed
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does what I showed count as evidence of my age` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a young person (under 18, or about to turn 18)` THEN
        IF `an authorised person has asked my age, or for evidence of it`
        THEN `yes if` (`Does this count as evidence of my age` `what I showed`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I be made to leave because I did not prove my age (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) s 126(1)(b)(ii))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `an authorised person has asked my age, or for evidence of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on licensed or regulated premises, the licensee, a manager, a staff member or a police officer has asked you to state your age or to show evidence of it (s 126)
      `the place` IS A Place @desc Where you are (or were)
      `the authorised person knows or reasonably suspects I am under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the authorised person knows, or suspects on reasonable grounds, that you are under 18
      `the age I stated is or appears false` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the age you stated is false, or appears to be false
      `what I showed` IS AN Evidence @desc What you showed
      `it proves I am 18 or over` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what you showed proves you are 18 or over
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I be made to leave because I did not prove my age` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a young person (under 18, or about to turn 18)` THEN
        IF `an authorised person has asked my age, or for evidence of it`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can I be made to leave for not proving my age` `the place` `the authorised person knows or reasonably suspects I am under 18` `the age I stated is or appears false` `what I showed` `it proves I am 18 or over`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can my ID be confiscated (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) s 126(2a), (2D))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `an authorised person has asked my age, or for evidence of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on licensed or regulated premises, the licensee, a manager, a staff member or a police officer has asked you to state your age or to show evidence of it (s 126)
      `what I showed` IS AN Evidence @desc What you showed
      `the authorised person reasonably suspects it is forged, false or counterfeit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the authorised person suspects, on reasonable grounds, that it is forged, false or counterfeit
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can my ID be confiscated by the authorised person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a young person (under 18, or about to turn 18)` THEN
        IF `an authorised person has asked my age, or for evidence of it`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can my ID be confiscated` `what I showed` `the authorised person reasonably suspects it is forged, false or counterfeit`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Have I committed an offence in answering a request for my age (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) s 126(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `an authorised person has asked my age, or for evidence of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on licensed or regulated premises, the licensee, a manager, a staff member or a police officer has asked you to state your age or to show evidence of it (s 126)
      `I failed to comply with the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you did not do what you were required to do (state your age, show evidence, or leave)
      `I had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had a reasonable excuse for not complying
      `what I said or showed was false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what you said or showed was false or misleading in a material respect (for example a fake ID)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Have I committed an offence in answering the request for my age` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a young person (under 18, or about to turn 18)` THEN
        IF `an authorised person has asked my age, or for evidence of it`
        THEN `yes if` (`Have I committed an offence answering the request for my age` `I failed to comply with the requirement` `I had a reasonable excuse` `what I said or showed was false or misleading`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Have I committed an offence by going back in (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) s 126(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been required to leave, or removed from, the premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were required to leave, or were removed from, licensed or regulated premises under s 126
      `I went back in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you went back into the premises
      `hours since I was made to leave` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours after being required to leave, or removed, you went back in
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Have I committed an offence by going back in within 24 hours` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a young person (under 18, or about to turn 18)` THEN
        IF `I have been required to leave, or removed from, the premises`
        THEN `yes if` (`Have I committed an offence by going back in` `I went back in` `hours since I was made to leave`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Penalties and infringement notices (s 167)`

@export What is the most I can be fined for this offence (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) ss 121, 122, 123, 126)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the offence` IS A `My offence` @desc The offence
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined for this juvenile offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a young person (under 18, or about to turn 18)` THEN `as an amount` (`What is the most I can be fined` `the offence`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export If I am given an infringement notice for this offence, how much does it ask me to pay (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) s 167(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the offence` IS A `My offence` @desc The offence
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much would an infringement notice ask me to pay` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a young person (under 18, or about to turn 18)` THEN `as an amount` (`What would an infringement notice ask me to pay` `the offence`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How many days do I have to pay an infringement notice (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) s 167(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Days`
`How many days would I have to pay an infringement notice` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a young person (under 18, or about to turn 18)` THEN `as days` (`How many days do I have to pay an infringement notice`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For a parent, guardian or other adult with a young person (ss 121(1), (3), (4), (9), 122(2), (3)(b), 122A, 124, 125)`

-- Division 9 puts these duties on "a person": the adult who supplies liquor (ss 121(1)(c), 122(2), 122A), buys it for a
-- juvenile who asks (s 121(3)), takes a juvenile on to premises as a responsible adult (ss 121(5)(a)(i), (9), 122(3)(b)),
-- or sends one to get liquor (s 124). The adult is taken to be 18 or over, as the role says.

§§§ `ss 121(1), (3), 122(2), 122A, 125(1)(b) -- giving or buying alcohol for a young person`

@export May I give alcohol to this young person here (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) ss 121(1), 122(2), 122A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have given, or would give, alcohol to a person under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have sold, supplied or given alcohol to a person under 18, or bought it for them, or are thinking of doing so (ss 121(1), (3), 122(2), 122A)
      `where the young person is given the alcohol` IS A Place @desc Where the young person is, or would be, given the alcohol
      `who I am to the young person` IS A `Who I am to the young person` @desc Whether you are the young person's parent or guardian, or another adult with or without their parent's or guardian's consent
      `the parent or guardian was drunk when consenting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the young person's parent or guardian was drunk when they gave consent
      `I am drunk when supplying` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are drunk (noticeably impaired speech, balance, coordination or behaviour, reasonably believed to come from liquor, s 3A(1)(b), (c))
      `the young person is drunk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the young person is drunk
      `I am able to supervise their drinking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are able to supervise the young person drinking it
      `a circumstance prescribed by the regulations applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a circumstance prescribed by the Liquor Control Regulations applies
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I give alcohol to this young person at this place` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent, guardian or other adult with a young person` THEN
        IF `I have given, or would give, alcohol to a person under 18`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is it lawful for this person to give me alcohol here` `where the young person is given the alcohol` (`the supplier for` `who I am to the young person`) `the parent or guardian was drunk when consenting` `I am drunk when supplying` `the young person is drunk` `I am able to supervise their drinking` `a circumstance prescribed by the regulations applies`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export If I sold or supplied liquor to a young person, could I rely on believing they were 18 (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) s 125(1)(b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have given, or would give, alcohol to a person under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have sold, supplied or given alcohol to a person under 18, or bought it for them, or are thinking of doing so (ss 121(1), (3), 122(2), 122A)
      `the young person's age` IS A NUMBER @desc The young person's age in whole years when it was sold or supplied
      `I believed on reasonable grounds they were 18 or over` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you believed, on reasonable grounds, that they were 18 or over
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Could I rely on believing the young person was 18` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent, guardian or other adult with a young person` THEN
        IF `I have given, or would give, alcohol to a person under 18`
        THEN `yes if` (`Could the seller rely on believing I was 18` `the young person's age` `I believed on reasonable grounds they were 18 or over`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is it an offence for me to buy or get liquor for a young person who asked me to, on licensed premises (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) s 121(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have given, or would give, alcohol to a person under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have sold, supplied or given alcohol to a person under 18, or bought it for them, or are thinking of doing so (ss 121(1), (3), 122(2), 122A)
      `where the young person is given the alcohol` IS A Place @desc Where the young person is, or would be, given the alcohol
      `I bought or got it for them at their request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you bought or got liquor for the young person because they asked
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is it an offence for me to buy liquor for a young person who asked me to` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent, guardian or other adult with a young person` THEN
        IF `I have given, or would give, alcohol to a person under 18`
        THEN `yes if` (`Have I committed an offence by getting someone to buy for me` `where the young person is given the alcohol` `I bought or got it for them at their request`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 121(4), (5), (9), 122(3)(b), 125(2)(b) -- taking a young person on to licensed or regulated premises`

-- The adult is taken to be 18 or over, as the role says, so the s 125(2)(b) "adult" fact is TRUE.
@export Am I a responsible adult for this young person (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) s 125(2)(b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am, or will be, with a person under 18 on licensed or regulated premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are taking, or have taken, a person under 18 on to licensed premises or regulated premises, such as a hotel, tavern, cafe or venue (ss 121(4), (5), (9), 122(3))
      `how I am related to the young person` IS A `How I am related to the young person` @desc How you are related to the young person
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I a responsible adult for this young person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent, guardian or other adult with a young person` THEN
        IF `I am, or will be, with a person under 18 on licensed or regulated premises`
        THEN `yes if` (`is a responsible adult` (`the companion for` `how I am related to the young person`) TRUE)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is it an offence for the young person (and the licensee) that the young person is on these licensed premises with me (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) s 121(4), (5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am, or will be, with a person under 18 on licensed or regulated premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are taking, or have taken, a person under 18 on to licensed premises or regulated premises, such as a hotel, tavern, cafe or venue (ss 121(4), (5), (9), 122(3))
      `the young person's reason for being there` IS A Reason @desc Why the young person is there (the choices are worded as the young person would say them)
      `how I am related to the young person` IS A `How I am related to the young person` @desc How you are related to the young person
      `I am supervising the young person there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are supervising the young person while they are there
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is it an offence for the young person to be on these licensed premises with me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent, guardian or other adult with a young person` THEN
        IF `I am, or will be, with a person under 18 on licensed or regulated premises`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is it an offence for me to be on licensed premises` `the young person's reason for being there` (`the companion for` `how I am related to the young person`) TRUE `I am supervising the young person there`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export If I leave the young person on the licensed premises, do I commit an offence (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) s 121(9))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am, or will be, with a person under 18 on licensed or regulated premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are taking, or have taken, a person under 18 on to licensed premises or regulated premises, such as a hotel, tavern, cafe or venue (ss 121(4), (5), (9), 122(3))
      `how I am related to the young person` IS A `How I am related to the young person` @desc How you are related to the young person
      `I am supervising the young person there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are supervising the young person while they are there
      `I leave without the young person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you leave the premises, or leave the young person without your company and supervision
      `I first told the licensee or a staff member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you told the licensee, or an employee or agent of the licensee, before you left
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is it an offence for me to leave the young person on the licensed premises` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent, guardian or other adult with a young person` THEN
        IF `I am, or will be, with a person under 18 on licensed or regulated premises`
        THEN `yes if` (`s 121(9) -- the responsible adult leaves the juvenile behind` (`the companion for` `how I am related to the young person`) `I am supervising the young person there` `I leave without the young person` `I first told the licensee or a staff member`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Having come with the young person as their responsible adult for a meal, is it an offence for me to take or keep them in this part of regulated premises (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) s 122(3)(b), (4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am, or will be, with a person under 18 on licensed or regulated premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are taking, or have taken, a person under 18 on to licensed premises or regulated premises, such as a hotel, tavern, cafe or venue (ss 121(4), (5), (9), 122(3))
      `the young person's reason for being there` IS A Reason @desc Why the young person is there (the choices are worded as the young person would say them)
      `liquor is sold or supplied where the young person is` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether liquor is sold or supplied in the part of the premises where the young person is
      `the young person works for the licensee, occupier or a contractor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the young person is an employee or agent of the licensee or occupier, or of someone working under a contract with them
      `I came as their responsible adult for a meal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you came with the young person as their responsible adult so that they could get a meal
      `I caused or permitted them to be there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you caused or permitted the young person to enter or stay in that part
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is it an offence for me to take the young person into this part of regulated premises` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent, guardian or other adult with a young person` THEN
        IF `I am, or will be, with a person under 18 on licensed or regulated premises`
        THEN `yes if` (`s 122(3)(b) -- the purported responsible adult commits the offence` `the young person's reason for being there` `liquor is sold or supplied where the young person is` `the young person works for the licensee, occupier or a contractor` `I came as their responsible adult for a meal` `I caused or permitted them to be there`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 124 -- sending a young person for liquor`

-- Asked of a sending, so the s 124 fact that the young person was sent is TRUE by the question's own terms.
@export Is it an offence for me to send this young person to get liquor (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) s 124)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have sent, or would send, a person under 18 to get liquor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have sent, or are thinking of sending, someone you know or believe to be under 18 to get liquor (s 124)
      `the place I send them to` IS A Place @desc Where you send, or sent, the young person
      `I know or believe they are under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you know or believe that the person you send is under 18
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is it an offence for me to send this young person to get liquor` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent, guardian or other adult with a young person` THEN
        IF `I have sent, or would send, a person under 18 to get liquor`
        THEN `yes if` (`Did the person who sent me commit an offence` `the place I send them to` TRUE `I know or believe they are under 18`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Penalties`

@export What is the most I can be fined for this offence about a young person (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) ss 121, 122, 122A, 124)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the adult offence` IS AN `Adult offence` @desc The offence
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined for this offence as an adult` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent, guardian or other adult with a young person` THEN `as an amount` (`the most an adult can be fined for` `the adult offence`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the licensee, a manager, or a person who sells or serves liquor (ss 121(1), (4), (10), (11), 122(2), 125, 126)`

-- The licensee, a manager and their staff are bound by ss 121(1), (2), (4), (10) and 122(2), and have the defences of
-- s 125(1)(b), (c). They are also "authorised persons" (s 3(1)), so the s 126 powers over a suspected juvenile are
-- theirs: what they may require is the young person's question asked the other way.

§§§ `ss 121(1), 122(2), 125(1)(b), (c) -- selling or supplying to a person under 18`

@export Is it an offence of mine that liquor is, or was, sold or supplied to a person under 18 here (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) ss 121(1), 122(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `liquor has been, or may be, sold or supplied to a person under 18 at my business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether liquor has been, or may be, sold or supplied to a person under 18 at your premises or by your business (ss 121(1), 122(2), 125)
      `where it is sold or supplied` IS A Place @desc Where the liquor is, or was, sold or supplied
      `my part in the sale` IS A `My part in the sale` @desc Your part: the licensee; the manager supervising the premises at the time; the person who sold or supplied it; a person who permitted it; or a staff member who had no part in it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is it an offence of mine that liquor is sold or supplied to this person under 18` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I hold a licence, manage licensed premises, or sell or serve liquor` THEN
        IF `liquor has been, or may be, sold or supplied to a person under 18 at my business`
        THEN `yes if` (`ss 121(1), 122(2) -- the sale or supply to a juvenile is an offence of mine` `where it is sold or supplied` `my part in the sale`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I rely on believing the person I sold or supplied liquor to was 18 (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) s 125(1)(b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `liquor has been, or may be, sold or supplied to a person under 18 at my business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether liquor has been, or may be, sold or supplied to a person under 18 at your premises or by your business (ss 121(1), 122(2), 125)
      `I sold or supplied it myself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the person who sold or supplied the liquor
      `the person's age when it was sold or supplied` IS A NUMBER @desc The person's age in whole years when it was sold or supplied
      `I believed on reasonable grounds the person was 18 or over` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you believed, on reasonable grounds, that the person was 18 or over
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I rely on believing the person was 18` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I hold a licence, manage licensed premises, or sell or serve liquor` THEN
        IF `liquor has been, or may be, sold or supplied to a person under 18 at my business`
        THEN `yes if` (`I sold or supplied it myself` AND (`Could the seller rely on believing I was 18` `the person's age when it was sold or supplied` `I believed on reasonable grounds the person was 18 or over`))
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export On regulated premises, where I did not sell or supply it myself, do I have the defence of not enticing juveniles and of proper diligence (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) s 125(1)(c))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `liquor has been, or may be, sold or supplied to a person under 18 at my business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether liquor has been, or may be, sold or supplied to a person under 18 at your premises or by your business (ss 121(1), 122(2), 125)
      `where it is sold or supplied` IS A Place @desc Where the liquor is, or was, sold or supplied
      `I am the licensee, occupier or a manager of the premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the licensee or occupier, or a manager, of the premises
      `I sold or supplied it myself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the person who sold or supplied the liquor
      `the business was not run to entice juveniles there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the business was not conducted in a way that would entice juveniles to the part where liquor was sold, supplied or drunk
      `proper diligence was exercised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether proper diligence was exercised to prevent liquor being sold, supplied or drunk in breach of Division 9 (for the court to decide; you must show it)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Do I have the defence for regulated premises` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I hold a licence, manage licensed premises, or sell or serve liquor` THEN
        IF `liquor has been, or may be, sold or supplied to a person under 18 at my business`
        THEN `yes if` (`s 125(1)(c) -- the defence for regulated premises` `where it is sold or supplied` `I am the licensee, occupier or a manager of the premises` `I sold or supplied it myself` `the business was not run to entice juveniles there` `proper diligence was exercised`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 121(4), (5) -- a person under 18 on the premises`

-- s 121(4) makes the licensee, a permitting employee or agent, and the juvenile each commit an offence on the same facts, and
-- s 121(5) excepts them all alike; so the baseline's juvenile question decides it, with the employee's permission added.
-- Whether the companion is an adult and whether they supervise are read by the baseline only together (s 121(5)(a)(i)),
-- so they are one input, which keeps the question within the form's probe (NOTES QA9).
@export Is it an offence of mine that a person under 18 enters or stays on this part of my licensed premises (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) s 121(4), (5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a person under 18 is, or wants to be, on my licensed premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a person under 18 is, or wants to be, on your licensed premises or a part of them (s 121(4), (5))
      `my part in the person's presence` IS A `My part in the young person's presence` @desc Whether you are the licensee, or a manager, employee or agent of the licensee who did or did not permit the person to enter or stay on that part of the premises
      `the person's reason for being there` IS A Reason @desc Why the person is there (the choices are worded as the young person would say them)
      `who is with the person` IS A `Who is with the young person` @desc Who is with the person
      `that person is an adult who is supervising them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person with them is an adult (18 or over) who is supervising them while they are there
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is it an offence of mine that this person under 18 is on this part of my licensed premises` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I hold a licence, manage licensed premises, or sell or serve liquor` THEN
        IF `a person under 18 is, or wants to be, on my licensed premises`
        THEN `yes if` (`s 121(4) -- the presence of the juvenile is an offence of mine` `my part in the person's presence` (`Is it an offence for me to be on licensed premises` `the person's reason for being there` (`the companion of theirs for` `who is with the person`) `that person is an adult who is supervising them` `that person is an adult who is supervising them`))
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 121(10), (11) -- employing a person under 18 to serve liquor`

@export Is it an offence for me to employ or engage this person under 18 to sell, supply or serve liquor (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) s 121(10), (11))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I employ, or would employ, a person under 18 to sell, supply or serve liquor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you employ or engage, or would, a person under 18 to sell, supply or serve liquor (s 121(10), (11))
      `the person's age` IS A NUMBER @desc The person's age in whole years
      `the person would only serve liquor with meals` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person would only serve liquor ancillary to a meal
      `the Director has approved the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Director of Liquor Licensing has approved the person's employment or engagement
      `the work is supervised at all times` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person's work is supervised at all times
      `the work is assessed for, or the person has completed, a prescribed training course` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work will be assessed for a prescribed training course the person is doing, or the person has completed one that assessed it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is it an offence for me to employ this person under 18 to sell, supply or serve liquor` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I hold a licence, manage licensed premises, or sell or serve liquor` THEN
        IF `I employ, or would employ, a person under 18 to sell, supply or serve liquor`
        THEN `yes if` (NOT (`May I be employed to serve liquor` `the person's age` `the person would only serve liquor with meals` `the Director has approved the employment` `the work is supervised at all times` `the work is assessed for, or the person has completed, a prescribed training course`))
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 126 -- asking a suspected juvenile's age`

-- Asked where the licensee or staff member knows or suspects on reasonable grounds that the person is under 18 (the
-- situation), so the s 126(1) fact is TRUE by the question's own terms.
@export As an authorised person, may I require this person to state their age (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) s 126(1)(a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I suspect a person on the premises is under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, as the licensee, a manager or a staff member, know or suspect on reasonable grounds that a person on the licensed or regulated premises is under 18 (s 126(1))
      `where the person is` IS A Place @desc Where the person is
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I require this person to state their age` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I hold a licence, manage licensed premises, or sell or serve liquor` THEN
        IF `I suspect a person on the premises is under 18`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can I be required to state my age` `where the person is` TRUE)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export As an authorised person, may I require this person to show evidence of their age (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) s 126(1)(b)(i))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I suspect a person on the premises is under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, as the licensee, a manager or a staff member, know or suspect on reasonable grounds that a person on the licensed or regulated premises is under 18 (s 126(1))
      `where the person is` IS A Place @desc Where the person is
      `the age the person stated is or appears false` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the age the person stated is false, or appears to be false
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I require this person to show evidence of their age` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I hold a licence, manage licensed premises, or sell or serve liquor` THEN
        IF `I suspect a person on the premises is under 18`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can I be required to show evidence of my age` `where the person is` TRUE `the age the person stated is or appears false`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does what the person showed count as evidence of their age (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) s 126(1)(b)(i), (2C))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I suspect a person on the premises is under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, as the licensee, a manager or a staff member, know or suspect on reasonable grounds that a person on the licensed or regulated premises is under 18 (s 126(1))
      `what the person showed` IS AN Evidence @desc What the person showed (the choices are worded as the young person would say them)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does what the person showed count as evidence of their age` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I hold a licence, manage licensed premises, or sell or serve liquor` THEN
        IF `I suspect a person on the premises is under 18`
        THEN `yes if` (`Does this count as evidence of my age` `what the person showed`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export As an authorised person, may I require this person to leave because they did not prove their age (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) s 126(1)(b)(ii))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I suspect a person on the premises is under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, as the licensee, a manager or a staff member, know or suspect on reasonable grounds that a person on the licensed or regulated premises is under 18 (s 126(1))
      `where the person is` IS A Place @desc Where the person is
      `the age the person stated is or appears false` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the age the person stated is false, or appears to be false
      `what the person showed` IS AN Evidence @desc What the person showed (the choices are worded as the young person would say them)
      `it proves the person is 18 or over` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what the person showed proves they are 18 or over
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I require this person to leave for not proving their age` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I hold a licence, manage licensed premises, or sell or serve liquor` THEN
        IF `I suspect a person on the premises is under 18`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can I be made to leave for not proving my age` `where the person is` TRUE `the age the person stated is or appears false` `what the person showed` `it proves the person is 18 or over`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export As an authorised person, may I confiscate what the person showed as evidence of their age (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) s 126(2a), (2D))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I suspect a person on the premises is under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, as the licensee, a manager or a staff member, know or suspect on reasonable grounds that a person on the licensed or regulated premises is under 18 (s 126(1))
      `what the person showed` IS AN Evidence @desc What the person showed (the choices are worded as the young person would say them)
      `I reasonably suspect it is forged, false or counterfeit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you suspect, on reasonable grounds, that it is forged, false or counterfeit
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I confiscate what the person showed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I hold a licence, manage licensed premises, or sell or serve liquor` THEN
        IF `I suspect a person on the premises is under 18`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can my ID be confiscated` `what the person showed` `I reasonably suspect it is forged, false or counterfeit`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Penalties`

@export What is the most I can be fined for this offence about a person under 18 (Liquor Control Act 1988 (WA) ss 121, 122)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the business offence` IS A `Business offence` @desc The offence, and your part in it
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined for this offence as a licensee or seller` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I hold a licence, manage licensed premises, or sell or serve liquor` THEN `as an amount` (`the most a licensee or seller can be fined for` `the business offence`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
